# Gitleaks false-positive allowlist.
#
# Every entry is a full fingerprint: <commit>:<file>:<rule-id>:<line>. The CI scan
# runs `gitleaks detect --log-opts HEAD`, which walks every commit reachable from
# HEAD, so a finding keeps being reported even after the offending file is rewritten
# or removed at the tip. An allowlist entry is the only way to clear it. The shorter
# <file>:<rule-id>:<line> form is silently ignored by gitleaks -- the commit hash is
# what anchors a fingerprint.
#
# 2026-07-13 -- rule "Password in URL", from the GitLab-customised ruleset that the
# pipelines repository hands to the second detection pass. Six matches, none of which
# commits a credential:
#
#   * github.go / gitlab.go -- the provider builds an authenticated clone URL by
#     splicing the token it holds at runtime (the `p.token` field) into the userinfo
#     position of the remote. The only literal in the source is the URL prefix; the
#     rule cannot tell that concatenation apart from a real password.
#
#   * github_test.go / gitlab_test.go -- BDD assertions covering that URL builder.
#     The provider under test is constructed with the literal placeholder
#     "my-token", which is what the expected URL therefore carries.
